\import{macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}

\taxon{Remark}
\title{Randomness, schedules, and stopping}
\tag{ftip}
\tag{optimization}

\p{We formulate a pretraining run as more than minimization of the empirical
objective #{L_N} in \ref{ftip-001E}. It includes the initialization, data order, window offsets, dropout and
other model randomness, numerical precision, distributed reduction order,
optimizer state, every hyperparameter schedule, and a stopping rule. These
objects determine a distribution over final parameters even when the source
mixture and nominal objective agree.}

\p{The training configuration of \citet{sec. 5.3}{vaswani2017attention} and
the scaling experiments of \citet{sec. 2.2}{kaplan2020scaling} report concrete
instances of these choices. A later theorem about optimization must state
which randomness it averages over and whether the stopping time is fixed or
data-dependent.}
